{"actions":[{"date":"2025-12-16","source":"House floor actions","text":"Referred to the Committee on Energy and Commerce, and in addition to the Committee on Ways and Means, for a period to be subsequently determined by the Speaker, in each case for consideration of such provisions as fall within the jurisdiction of the committee concerned.","type":"IntroReferral"},{"date":"2025-12-16","source":"House floor actions","text":"Referred to the Committee on Energy and Commerce, and in addition to the Committee on Ways and Means, for a period to be subsequently determined by the Speaker, in each case for consideration of such provisions as fall within the jurisdiction of the committee concerned.","type":"IntroReferral"},{"date":"2025-12-16","source":"Library of Congress","text":"Introduced in House","type":"IntroReferral"},{"date":"2025-12-16","source":"Library of Congress","text":"Introduced in House","type":"IntroReferral"}],"amendments":{"items":[],"total":0},"analysis_status":"scored","bipartisan_band":null,"chamber":"House","committees":[{"activities":[{"date":"2025-12-16","name":"Referred To"}],"chamber":"House","code":"hswm00","name":"Ways and Means Committee","subcommittees":[]},{"activities":[{"date":"2025-12-16","name":"Referred To"}],"chamber":"House","code":"hsif00","name":"Energy and Commerce Committee","subcommittees":[]}],"cosponsor_count":160,"fetched_at":"2026-10-26T06:18:56+00:00","history":[{"day":"2026-10-26","importance":60,"viability":40.0}],"id":"119-hr-6766","importance":60,"importance_band":"moderate","importance_detail":{"consistent":true,"dimension_mean":59.0,"dimensions":[{"assessment":"Affects nursing home residents, their designated essential caregivers, and staff across Medicare skilled nursing facilities, Medicaid nursing facilities, and other specified facilities nationwide.","evidence":"an estimated 1,300,000 individuals resided in nursing homes in 2020 at the onset of the COVID-19 pandemic","evidence_verified":true,"key":"population","score":70},{"assessment":"Directly impacts the well-being and visitation rights of residents and caregivers during emergencies, preventing isolation while introducing strict compliance and appeal rules.","evidence":"Many long-term care residents declined dramatically or died prematurely from failure to thrive in isolation.","evidence_verified":false,"key":"magnitude","score":65},{"assessment":"Introduces civil money penalties up to $5,000 for non-compliance and administrative costs for state survey agencies to investigate appeals, but no direct federal appropriations are specified.","evidence":"impose a civil money penalty in an amount to be determined by the agency (not to exceed $5,000)","evidence_verified":true,"key":"fiscal","score":30},{"assessment":"Amends titles XVIII and XIX of the Social Security Act to create new statutory rights, facility requirements, and a federal regulatory appeals process.","evidence":"To amend titles XVIII and XIX of the Social Security Act to require skilled nursing facilities","evidence_verified":true,"key":"scope","score":60},{"assessment":"Permanent statutory changes taking effect two years after enactment, applying whenever regular visitation is restricted during future emergencies.","evidence":"The amendments made by this Act shall take effect on the date that is 2 years after the date of enactment of this Act","evidence_verified":true,"key":"duration","score":70}],"missing_information":["Exact federal administrative costs for establishing the appeals process","Specific staffing budget adjustments needed for state survey agencies"],"rationale":"The bill establishes mandatory access rights for essential caregivers in certain long-term care facilities during emergencies, affecting residents, caregivers, and facilities nationwide with specific administrative and enforcement mechanisms.","score":60},"importance_meta":{"generated_at":"2026-10-26T06:59:47+00:00","model":"gemini-3.5-flash-lite","source_basis":"text+summary","source_urls